_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 21
---
order: 21
---
short_label: VIII.21
---
statement: If two mean proportional numbers fall between two numbers, then the numbers are similar solid numbers.
---
proof:

Let two mean proportional numbers *C* and *D* fall between the two numbers *A* and *B.*

I say that *A* and *B* are similar solid numbers.

Take three numbers *E, F,* and *G,* the least of those which have the same ratio with *A, C,* and *D.* Then the extremes of them *E* and *G* are relatively prime. [!just VII.33; VIII.2, VIII.3]

